criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:• Heterosexual couples in monogamous stable relationships (\>6 months);

* Both male and female participants are required to have \>18 years old prior to entering the study;
* Eligible men are those with a prior vasectomy and documented azoospermia on semen analysis prior to the baseline visit;
* Patients must provide a signed and dated informed consent form, indicating their understanding and agreement to participate;
* Patients must be willing to comply with all study procedures and be available for the duration of the study period;
* Both male and female participants are required to have prior experience using a male condom during intercourse;
* All participants (both male and female) must be in good general health based on their medical history and physical examination. At study entry, male participants must have no open penile lesions or lacerations as confirmed by genital exam, and female participants must have no vaginal lesions or lacerations as confirmed by vaginal exam. Participants with significant genital findings at baseline will not be included in this study.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Participants will be excluded if they do not meet any of the inclusion criteria. Exclusion criteria comprise:

  * Couples who are not heterosexual or monogamous;
  * Relationships lasting less than six months;
  * Individuals under 18 years of age;
  * Male participants who have not undergone a prior vasectomy or who do not have a semen analysis confirming azoospermia before the baseline visit;
  * Inability or unwillingness to provide signed and dated informed consent;
  * Inability to comply with all study procedures;
  * Unavailability for the full duration of the study;
  * Either partner lacking prior experience with male condom use during intercourse;
  * Presence of penile or vaginal lesions or lacerations in either partner, detected during medical physical examination;
